Hey all,

I was finally able to solve the problem by downloading the source package and installing from the command line with R CMD INSTALL instead of using install.packages() or inla.upgrade() from inside R. Yay!

One further note for those using homebrew on Macs, I ran into further errors because the formulae on homebrew <https://formulae.brew.sh/formula/r> build R against OpenBLAS. You can avoid this by installing the cask version <https://formulae.brew.sh/cask/r>.

Happly INLAing!

Simon

